# operator_extend.skill — CDLC Context Package
# KQLBridge v0.1 | Generate → Test → Distribute → Observe
# ============================================================

## What extend does in KQL
Adds computed columns to the result set without dropping existing ones.
Equivalent to SELECT *, expr AS alias in SQL.

## Translation table
| KQL                                      | Spark SQL                                    |
|------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------|
| T | extend double = value * 2            | SELECT *, (value * 2) AS double FROM T        |
| T | extend IsLarge = Amount > 1000       | SELECT *, (Amount > 1000) AS IsLarge FROM T   |
| T | extend a = x + 1, b = y - 1         | SELECT *, (x + 1) AS a, (y - 1) AS b FROM T  |

## Full examples
```kql
Orders | extend Profit = Revenue - Cost | where Profit > 0
```
```sql
SELECT *
FROM (SELECT *, (Revenue - Cost) AS Profit FROM Orders) t
WHERE Profit > 0
```
Note: chained extend+where is simplified in v0.1 to a flat SELECT.

## Edge cases
- Boolean extend (v0.1 supported): `extend IsActive = Status == "active"` renders as scalar comparison
- Multiple assignments in one extend: all rendered as additional SELECT cols
- Extend after project: only projected cols are base; extended col appended

## Known limits
- Extending with a subquery is NOT supported in v0.1
- Self-referencing extend (`extend b = a + 1, c = b * 2`) renders literally; SQL engines evaluate left-to-right

## Routing rules
- extend_op → SUPPORTED → SparkSQLGenerator._build_body() ExtendOp branch
- Comparison in extend → assign_comparison grammar rule → Comparison AST node
